{title: Be Silent Before God}
{subtitle: Psalms 62:5–6}
{key: Gm}
{tempo: 86}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Gm7] | ×9

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
My soul waits in silence for God alone
From him comes my sal[Cm7]vation
He alone is my rock and my salva[Ebmaj7]tion
My stronghold [D7]I will never be [Gm7]badly shaken
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Cm7]Be silent before God alone my soul
[Gm7]For my hope comes from him
[Cm7]He alone is my rock and my salvation
My [Ebmaj7]stronghold [D7]I will not be [Gm7]shaken
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
They plot only to bring him down from his high place
They take pleasure in falsehood
With their [Cm7]mouths they bless but inwardly they curse
[Ebmaj7]How long will you [D7]all as[Gm7]sail a man
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Be si[Cm7]lent before God alone my soul
For my [Gm7]hope comes from him
[Cm7]He alone is my rock and my salvation
[Ebmaj7]My strong[D7]hold I will not [Gm7]be shaken
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
My sal[Cm7]vation and my honor rest on God
My [Gm7]mighty rock my refuge is in God
[Cm7]Trust in him at all times you people
[Ebmaj7]Pour [D7]out your hearts be[Gm7]fore him
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Be si[Cm7]lent before God alone my soul
For my [Gm7]hope comes from him
He [Cm7]alone is my rock and my salvation
[Ebmaj7]My strong[D7]hold I will not [Gm7]be shaken [Cm7]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
God is our re[Gm7]fuge [Cm7]
Se[Gm7]lah
